<div class="deck">

<div class="slide" id="s1">
  <p class="sn">01 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; What the Sunlake Blvd project would build</p>
  <h2>The county plans a new road of about {% fact "sunlake.length-miles.south" %} miles, from Center Village Drive to south of Appenzeller Boulevard.</h2>
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% fact "sunlake.length-miles.south" %}</div><div class="k">Miles, the county&#8217;s piece</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% fact "sunlake.design.south.lanes-interim" %}</div><div class="k">Lanes at first (interim)</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% fact "sunlake.design.south.lanes-ultimate" %}</div><div class="k">Lanes in the end (ultimate)</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% fact "sunlake.design.south.row-feet" %}</div><div class="k">Feet of right-of-way from Bexley North</div></div>
  </div>
  <p>The design solicitation describes two stages. The <strong>interim</strong> road has one lane each way and a turn lane &#8220;when warranted&#8221;, with a bike lane and a meandering multi-use trail. The <strong>ultimate</strong> road adds lanes, bike lanes and a sidewalk alongside the trail. The solicitation doesn&#8217;t say what would trigger the change from one to the other.</p>
  <p>The land comes from the <strong>Bexley North</strong> development, which will dedicate the right-of-way for the extension.</p>
  <p class="foot">Pasco County design solicitation RSQ-BW-26-019 &#183; Commission agenda, 2 June 2026</p>
</div>

<div class="slide" id="s2">
  <p class="sn">02 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; The bigger picture</p>
  <h2>Three pieces, planned and paid for separately, would close the gap in Sunlake Boulevard.</h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step now"><span class="st">Center Village Dr to south of Appenzeller Blvd</span><span class="sm">County &#183; MPO 454568-1 &#183; being designed</span></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="st">South of Appenzeller Blvd to south of Wilton Way</span><span class="sm">The Angeline developer&#8217;s piece</span></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="st">South of Wilton Way to Anchor Dune Dr</span><span class="sm">A line in the county capital plan</span></div>
  </div>
  <p>Sunlake already connects North Dale Mabry Highway in Hillsborough County with Center Village Drive, and separately runs north from south of Wilton Way to State Road 52. The middle piece is &#8220;being designed and will be constructed by Len-Angeline, LLC,&#8221; according to the county&#8217;s solicitation. The county is also building Ridge Road east from Sunlake Boulevard to US 41 under a design-build contract.</p>
  <p class="notyet">No project sheet for Sunlake was found in the MPO&#8217;s 2050 long range plan appendix, and no corridor-wide study has been published.</p>
  <p class="foot">Design solicitation RSQ-BW-26-019 &#183; FY 2026 adopted budget &#183; Commission agendas, 2025&#8211;2026</p>
</div>

<div class="slide" id="s3">
  <p class="sn">03 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; What kind of road</p>
  <h2>The design drawings label it a {% fact "sunlake.design.south.classification" %}, posted at {% fact "sunlake.design.south.posted-speed" %} mph.</h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step"><span class="st">Local road</span><span class="sm">Short trips, reaching the properties on it</span></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="st">Collector</span><span class="sm">Moderate volume, trips and speed</span></div>
    <div class="step now"><span class="st">Minor arterial</span><span class="sm">Feeds and augments a principal arterial</span></div>
    <div class="step now"><span class="st">Principal arterial</span><span class="sm">The highest-volume corridors</span></div>
  </div>
  <p>The typical sections label the road an arterial without saying minor or principal, so both are marked. They give a design speed of {% fact "sunlake.design.south.design-speed" %} mph and a posted speed of {% fact "sunlake.design.south.posted-speed" %} mph.</p>
  <p class="notyet">Whether the road is on the county&#8217;s Freight Priority Network, and what share of its traffic is expected to be trucks, hasn&#8217;t been published.</p>
  <p class="foot">Design solicitation RSQ-BW-26-019, typical sections &#183; Fla. Stat. 334.03</p>
</div>

<div class="slide" id="s4">
  <p class="sn">04 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; Process</p>
  <h2>The county is hiring a firm to design its piece. No route study or workshop has been published.</h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step"><span class="st">In county plans</span><span class="sm">MPO priority list &#183; capital plan</span></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="st">Route study</span><span class="sm">Named for FY 2026 &#183; none published</span></div>
    <div class="step now"><span class="st">Design</span><span class="sm">Now &#183; firm being hired</span></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="st">Right of way</span><span class="sm">Funded FY 2027</span></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="st">Construction</span><span class="sm">Funded FY 2028&#8211;2029</span></div>
  </div>
  <p>On {% fact "sunlake.schedule.south.design-shortlist" %} the Commission approved a ranked shortlist of three design firms and let the County Administrator negotiate and sign the contract. The signed contract hadn&#8217;t appeared on an agenda by 28 September 2026.</p>
  <p>The MPO&#8217;s June 2026 priority list gives the funded phase as {% fact "sunlake.schedule.south.funded-phase" %}, and its status column records design in FY 2026, right-of-way in FY 2027 and construction in FY 2028&#8211;2029, all in the county&#8217;s capital plan. The list places it under the heading &#8220;construction unfunded&#8221;, as it does Rangeland Boulevard.</p>
  <p class="foot">Pasco MPO 2026 List of Project Priorities &#183; Commission agenda, 2 June 2026</p>
</div>

<div class="slide" id="s5">
  <p class="sn">05 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; Cost and funding</p>
  <h2>No cost estimate has been published. The county&#8217;s capital plan lists {% sumM "sunlake.funding.south.fy2026", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2027", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2028", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2029", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2030", "sunlake.funding.south.future" %} for its piece.</h2>
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% sumM "sunlake.funding.south.fy2026", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2027", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2028", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2029", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2030", "sunlake.funding.south.future" %}</div><div class="k">County&#8217;s piece, all years</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.fy2026" %}</div><div class="k">Of that, adopted for FY 2026</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v">{% sumM "sunlake.funding.angeline.fy2026", "sunlake.funding.north.fy2026" %}</div><div class="k">The two northern lines, FY 2026</div></div>
  </div>
  <p>Only the first year is appropriated; the later years are the county&#8217;s planned amounts. The lines aren&#8217;t split by phase. The budget document doesn&#8217;t say how the two northern lines relate to the developer&#8217;s work on the Angeline piece.</p>
  <details class="xp">
    <summary>See every year</summary>
    <div class="tw"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>County capital plan</th><th class="n">Amount</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td colspan="2"><strong>North of Bud Bexley Pkwy to south of the Angeline line</strong> (the county&#8217;s piece)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2026 &#8212; adopted</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.fy2026" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2027 &#8212; proposed</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.fy2027" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2028 &#8212; proposed</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.fy2028" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2029 &#8212; proposed</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.fy2029" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2030 &#8212; proposed</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.fy2030" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Future years, after FY 2030</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.south.future" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>All years</strong></td><td class="n"><strong>{% sumM "sunlake.funding.south.fy2026", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2027", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2028", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2029", "sunlake.funding.south.fy2030", "sunlake.funding.south.future" %}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td colspan="2"><strong>South of the Angeline line to south of Wilton Way</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2026 &#8212; adopted (nothing in later years)</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.angeline.fy2026" %}</td></tr>
        <tr><td colspan="2"><strong>South of Wilton Way to Anchor Dune Dr</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>FY 2026 &#8212; adopted (nothing in later years)</td><td class="n">{% fact "sunlake.funding.north.fy2026" %}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </details>
  <p class="foot">Pasco County FY 2026 Adopted Budget &#183; FY 2026&#8211;2030 Capital Improvement Plan, printed page 124</p>
</div>

<div class="slide" id="s6">
  <p class="sn">06 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; Not yet published</p>
  <h2>Traffic, noise and environmental figures haven&#8217;t been published for this corridor.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Traffic:</strong> no counts, forecasts or intersection grades for this stretch of Sunlake.</li>
    <li><strong>Noise:</strong> no noise study.</li>
    <li><strong>Environment:</strong> no wetlands figures or environmental ratings.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are the figures a route study usually publishes. They&#8217;ll appear here, the same way as Rangeland&#8217;s, if one is.</p>
  <p class="foot">As of 28 September 2026</p>
</div>

<div class="slide" id="s7">
  <p class="sn">07 &nbsp;&#183;&nbsp; What to do</p>
  <h2>Questions worth asking</h2>
  <ol class="qlist">
    <li><b>Will a route study be published, with alternatives and a public workshop,</b> before design is fixed? The priority list names one for FY 2026; design procurement began in December 2025.</li>
    <li><b>What traffic is forecast</b> on the new road and on Bud Bexley Pkwy and Center Village Dr, with and without it, and how do nearby intersections grade?</li>
    <li><b>What would trigger widening from the interim road to six lanes,</b> and who decides?</li>
    <li><b>Has noise been studied</b> for homes along the Bexley North and Angeline stretches, and will mitigation be considered?</li>
    <li><b>What do the two northern budget lines pay for,</b> given the solicitation says the developer is designing and building the Angeline piece?</li>
    <li><b>What truck share is assumed,</b> and is the road on the Freight Priority Network?</li>
  </ol>
  <p style="margin-top:14px">No public workshop or comment period for Sunlake has been announced. Until one is, the County Commission takes public comment at its regular meetings, and its agendas are searchable at <strong>pascocofl.portal.civicclerk.com</strong> &#8212; that&#8217;s where the signed design contract should appear. If a figure here doesn&#8217;t match its source, tap it and use the link in the box, or <a href="{{ site.dispute_form.url }}">use the error-report form</a>.</p>
  <p class="foot">Board of County Commissioners &#183; pascocofl.portal.civicclerk.com</p>
</div>

